Create a docker-compose.yaml at the base of the checkout that starts up
the test environment.  The tests no longer need an "environment"
checkout to run.  Other modifications that go along with this.

This should make it possible (by not building the "test-shell" target of
the docker-compose file) to build images without needing to install
galsim, which will *hopefully* make it possible to do *something* in the
native architecture on a Mac.  (You still won't be able to run all the
snappl tests on a Mac, because some of them need galsim to run.)
